WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:02.240
- All right, y'all, it's almost
time to roll the credits,

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.800
but I wanna squeeze in
one last, very cool story.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.966
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.966 --> 00:00:08.088
(cheerful music)

00:00:08.088 --> 00:00:08.970
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.200
So you may not realize,

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.930
but nearly three million grandparents

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.520
are raising their own grandkids.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:14.670
God bless 'em.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.560
Still many of them struggle to get by.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.140
So a woman in Las Vegas is
trying to make it easier

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.950
for grandparents in her community

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.460
through a program called "Grants 4 Grands"

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.850
which is the cutest program title.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.858
Let's welcome Joyce, everybody.

00:00:27.858 --> 00:00:29.356
(audience cheering)

00:00:29.356 --> 00:00:30.189
Hi, Joyce.

00:00:31.887 --> 00:00:32.720
Hi.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.720
So this was born

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.640
out of another community
effort you led, right?

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.180
- Yes, it's Lace, the
nonprofit organization,

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.130
and we assist new needy
families and needy individuals

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:46.360
with emergency food and hygiene items.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:50.010
About 15 years ago, we
noticed there was a increase

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:53.180
of grandparents coming to get assistance.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:58.030
And so out of that, I created
the project "Grants 4 Grands"

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:00.560
so that we could assist these grandparents

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.200
that needed a little extra help.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.910
They may have been
eligible for food stamps,

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:10.480
but you can't buy Pampers
and soap and deodorants

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.020
and over-the-counter medications

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.490
and the other household
items that were needed.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:19.130
So we would give these grand families

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:23.100
a small monetary grant
to help do those things

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.690
and buy the things that they needed

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.148
that they couldn't get
with the food stamps.

00:01:26.148 --> 00:01:26.981
(audience applauding)

00:01:26.981 --> 00:01:28.707
- That's really amazing.

00:01:28.707 --> 00:01:31.190
The project has, it's
had its ups and downs,

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.710
but you're dedicated to
keep it going, right?

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:34.920
- Oh yeah, it's been rough

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.620
because we're, all of our
finances are generated

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.623
through donations, contributions.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.067
And so, there have been
times I'm thinking,

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:45.980
"This has got to end, we
can't do it any longer."

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.500
Then about five years ago,

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.670
a grandmother with a little
five year old grandson came in

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.170
and as I was preparing the food for them,

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.440
he was drawing this little picture.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.550
Well, he gave me the picture

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.510
and it was a picture of a rainbow.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:04.080
At one end of the rainbow
was a bag of food.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.440
The other end of the rainbow
was a little stick figure lady.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.440
And that, he said that was me.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.060
- [Kelly] Oh.
- And it just touched my heart

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.225
that his gold of that rainbow at the pot,

00:02:15.225 --> 00:02:17.060
the gold at the end of the pot,

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.700
was just a bag of food.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.880
So God told me no, it's
not time to stop this.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.480
The assignment is not over.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:26.615
We must continue to try and
help these grand families.

00:02:26.615 --> 00:02:28.820
(audience cheering)
- Oh my gosh, that was...

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:32.290
Did you hold it together
when you saw that drawing?

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:35.160
'Cause I'm not doing well, Joyce.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.420
That was so sweet.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.400
Oh my gosh.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.600
And that's gotta make you feel good.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.230
You know you're on the
right path, you know?

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.220
When something like that happens,

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.730
you know that you're supposed to be,

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:43.630
this is what you're,

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.920
you're the vessel for it, you know?

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.230
And that's a beautiful
thing to be reminded of,

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.550
especially when things get hard

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:49.480
and you're trying to help people.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.070
So thank you so much, Joyce.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.525
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:52.525 --> 00:02:54.410
(audience applauding)

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:55.780
And that's not all, Joyce.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:58.480
Our season long partner,
pilot pen makers of FriXion,

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.060
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.010
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.160
and just being awesome, just like you.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.790
So they're gonna give you $1,000.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:07.712
How's that sound?

00:03:07.712 --> 00:03:09.320
(audience cheering)

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.380
- Oh my goodness. Thank you so much.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.500
Much needed and much appreciated.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.333
- All right.

00:03:14.333 --> 00:03:16.090
Hey Joyce, I'm gonna throw

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.120
in an extra thousand dollars as well.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.225
'Cause I just think what
you're doing is really cool.

00:03:20.225 --> 00:03:21.110
(audience applauding)

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:22.292
Thank you so much for joining us!

00:03:22.292 --> 00:03:23.125
- Thanks so much.

00:03:23.125 --> 00:03:23.970
- And thank you

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.970
- for what you do, Joyce.
- We appreciate that.

